PROJECT_AUDIT*
# scripts/* rather than scripts/, because git does not descend into an excluded
# directory and a later negation cannot pull a file back out of one. lighthouse.mjs
# is the only file in there and package.json exposes it as `bun run lighthouse`,
# so leaving it untracked meant that script failed on every clone but this one.
scripts/*
!scripts/lighthouse.mjs
# CI runs generate-pricing.ts --check on every PR to catch drift between the Go
# fee table and pricing.ts. The blanket scripts/ ignore above kept it out of the
# repo, so that step would fail on a fresh checkout with the file missing.
!apps/payment-service/scripts/
coverage/
# All PDFs, anywhere. Real CVs get dropped in the repo root to test the parser
# against a genuine document, and they carry PII - name, phone, employment
# history. docs/*.pdf alone did not cover the root, so a stray `git add .` would
# have committed one into history permanently.
*.xlsx
*.csv
*Proposal.md
*TestCase.md
FINANCIAL-AUDIT.md
PLAN-brd-prd.md
*.pdf
.env.production
ARCHITECTURE-REVIEW.md

# Go build artifacts
apps/payment-service/payment-service
apps/notification-service/notification-service
apps/admin-service/admin-service
*.exe

# Coverage artifacts written by CI and by make test-go / test-python
coverage.out
coverage.xml
secrets/
*-sa.json

# Go coverage profiles, written by every local test run.
apps/*/cover.out
